issue.description:
Refine the UI Effects helper note so it appears only when an effect is selected and can vary by effect in the future.

## Overall direction

The current helper copy under the UI Effects selector is always visible and is written specifically for Tactile.

Change this to an effect-specific helper pattern.

For the current Tactile effect, show:

**Applied to secondary buttons and tabs.**

with a small info icon at the start.

When Effect = Off, do not show any helper note.

Future effects may use different helper copy depending on what they affect, so the helper should be driven by the selected effect rather than hard-coded globally.

## 1. Conditional visibility

Behavior:

### Effect = Off

* render no helper note;
* do not leave empty vertical space where the helper would normally appear.

### Effect = Tactile

Show the helper row:

**Applied to secondary buttons and tabs.**

The note should appear directly below or near the Effect select, consistent with the current layout.

## 2. Add info icon

Add a small information icon at the start of the helper row.

Requirements:

* use the existing accepted icon library;
* use a standard info/info-circle style icon;
* do not create a custom SVG;
* keep the icon visually subtle;
* align it vertically with the helper text;
* use a restrained gap between icon and text;
* preserve accessibility semantics appropriate for decorative/supporting helper text.

## 3. Helper text styling

Keep the helper visually secondary.

Requirements:

* use existing muted/helper text styling;
* preserve current Body/Sans typography conventions;
* do not make it look like an alert or validation message;
* do not add background, border, card surface, or extra chrome;
* keep the row compact.

## 4. Future effect support

Structure the helper behavior so each effect can define its own optional note.

Conceptually:

* Off → no note
* Tactile → "Applied to secondary buttons and tabs."
* future effects → their own effect-specific note, if needed

Do not add any new effect options in this ticket.

Do not build a generalized content-management layer. A simple effect-to-helper mapping is sufficient.

## 5. Preserve UI Effects behavior

Do not change:

* Off / Tactile options;
* Strength behavior;
* Secondary Button tactile semantics;
* TabsList tactile ring behavior;
* Theme v3;
* persisted UI Effects state;
* history/reset;
* import/export;
* Design Command;
* mutation operations;
* public registry.

This ticket is presentation/conditional-helper behavior only.

## Acceptance

* No helper note is shown when Effect = Off.
* No empty helper spacing remains when Off is selected.
* When Effect = Tactile, the note reads exactly:
  * `Applied to secondary buttons and tabs.`
* A small existing-library info icon appears at the start of the note.
* Icon and text are visually aligned and styled as subtle helper content.
* The helper is driven by the selected effect so future effects can use different optional notes.
* No new effect options, dependencies, schema changes, network behavior, or unrelated UI changes are introduced.
